wallpaper-manager (2.0.9.0-8~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.9).
  * Improvements have been made to a couple of details: if a user changes their background, the random cycling feature does not trigger immediately; instead, it waits for the established cycle interval.
  * If no background is selected, the random cycling feature will trigger upon closing the menu, provided that "Cycling" is enabled.
  * A fix was applied so that if the "BOXES" (the colored background container for text) is removed from text that had been set to a black color, the text remains black.
  * The "Font Selector" box and the method for changing fonts have been fixed.
  * Fixed a bug where the autostart .desktop file was left behind during the postrm phase.
  * EN ESPAÑOL: aquí ↓
  * Hubieron mejoras en un par de detalles;  si el usuario cambia su fondo no lanzamos el ciclado random, de inmediato, espera el tiempo de ciclo establecido.
  * Y si no elige ningún fondo de pantalla, al cerrar y está activo el "Ciclar", sí se lanza, un random.
  * Se reparó que al sacar el BOXES (caja de color del fondo del texto) a un texto que se haya contrastado en negro, permanece negro.
  * Se reparó la caja de "Selector de tipografías", y el método de cambio de fuente tipográfica.
  * Se reparó un bug, de haber dejado el archivo .desktop, del autostar, en postrm


  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.8).
  * For render_guardado.py, the calculation is now performed automatically for the text box.
  * Text contrast has been addressed for light images with black text (and vice versa). Additionally, a bug involving the shell call; `sh` was being used instead of `bash`: Fixed.
  * Little bug on the installer: Fixed.
  * EN ESPAÑOL: aquí ↓
  * Para render_guardado.py, hace el cálculo automático a la caja de texto.
  * Ahora el contraste del texto en imágenes claras, con texto negro, y viceversa. Y, había un bug de el llamado en shell, con `sh` y correspondía `bash`: Reparado.
  * Pequeño error en el instalador: Reparado.
  * Just a little bug, on the installer, caused the nautilus script, files, omission: Fixed.
  * Add the file on rotative wallpaper, to history.

  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.7)
  * You can now set up a rotation for quotes and/or wallpapers, with an optional autostart feature. With the settings we used to edit the appointment. Improvements have been made to quote downloading for other languages. New dependency: the `yad` command.
  * If you want to do some development work, the script `/usr/share/wallpaper_manager/Buenas_imágenes_citas/new_authors_banks.py` is available. It handles downloading *all* quotes for a given author—specifically those from az-quotes listed in `autores_completos_db.json`—using the same method employed for "Sri Sri Ravi Shankar." It might become editable in future versions via a "Select default authors" feature; that functionality is close to completion and wouldn't take much effort to implement.
  * EN ESPAÑOL: aquí ↓
  * Actualización a wallpaper-con-citas, para (1.2.6)
  * Ahora tiene para poner a ciclar; citas y/o wallpapers. Con la configuración que hayamos editado la cita. Y opcional en autostart. Mejoras en descarga de las citas para otros idiomas. Nueva dependencia: comando `yad`.
  * Si quieres desarrollar, tienes, el script "/usr/share/wallpaper_manager/Buenas_imágenes_citas/new_authors_banks.py". Dispone la descarga de *todas* las citas de un autor, que exista en "autores_completos_db.json"; los que corresponden, a az-quotes. Y usa el mismo método de "Sri Sri Ravi Shankar", tal vez quede editable en próximas versiones, a modo de "Elegir autores por defecto", ya está cerca, y es poco trabajo para lograrlo.

  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.4):
  * An ONLINE/OFFLINE toggle is added to the GTK interface. Turning it off cancels the download, and it loads local images in batches of 25 from: ~/$PICTURES/wallpaper manager_citas. 
  * You can upload a local folder to batch-upload personal images: + Folder
  * Se agrega un ONLINE - OFFLINE, en GTK. Y que al apagar, cancela la descargar, y cargue de a 25 imágenes locales, de: ~/Imágenes/wallpaper manager_citas
  * Se puede cargar una carpeta local, para cargar imágenes en lote personal: + Folder

  * Add white text to a dark image — black text to a light image. Agregué texto blanco a imagen oscura — texto negro a imagen clara; on wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.4).  

  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.3). The scripts for the booth—`prem_rawat_quotes.py` and `sadhguru_quotes.py`—had not been included in the package: Fixed. And a few details about the Python method. The teachers wanted to spark a thirst for knowledge 😉 It’s all sorted out now—thanks to them. I hope you enjoy it!
  * Atualización en wallpaper-con-citas, to (1.2.3). Los scripts para el stand —`prem_rawat_quotes.py` y `sadhguru_quotes.py`— no se habían incluido en el paquete; corregido. Y algún detalle del método python. Los maestros querían generar la sed de sabiduría 😉 Ya se arregló, a ellos gracias. Espero que disfruten! 

  * A minor bug was fixed; the CONFIG_FONT file (containing the "selected font") is ignored if set to `false`, so `FONTE_DEFAULT` is not used, on wallpaper-con-citas (1.2.2).
  * 1.2.1 Error fixed: the translation file that had been lost was recovered. 
  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas (1.2.0). The language flag—which allows switching between English and Spanish—now also supports: Arabic, Bengali, German, Greek, Persian (Iran), French, Gujarati, Hindi, Indonesian, Italian, Japanese, Lithuanian, Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Slovak, Tamil, Thai, Ukrainian, Simplified Chinese, and Traditional Chinese.
  * ☝️ These languages ​​are available on the Sadhguru and Prem Rawat websites.
  * For Siva P. and Sri Sri Ravi Shankar—as well as the "Other authors"—we use the `translate` command.
  * It also remembers the selected language upon restarting.
  * The font selector now includes thumbnails showing the font icon, providing a visual reference for the typeface's style. You can also configure it to remember your chosen font upon restarting, or it will default to: `./fonts/C059-BdIta.t1`. Hope you enjoy it.

  * Up to date on wallpaper-con-citas (1.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium
  * Enabled the background-change entry in the history list under "Set as wallpaper." Configured the "Other authors" search input field to trigger a random search. Fixed the "Info" window to include active links. ~*Final touches*~
  * Se activó el registro de cambio de fondo en la lista hitorial, en "Set as wallpaper". Se activó que si el campo de entrada de texto la búsqueda de "Otros autores", se genere un búsqueda aleatoria. Se reparó la ventana de "Info" con links activos. ~*Úlitmos retoques*~

  * Second upload. Improving the interface. Bug fixes - If the quote is disabled, do not display the empty text box; instead, it should remain empty unless "Edit text" is selected. Allow closing the image editing window with Ctrl+W, and the main window with Ctrl+Q. Refine the code so that the Prem quote output includes the event venue name, if mentioned.
  * The Prem quotes might be getting blocked due to too many requests. We are now loading them locally from the `banco.json` file. And minor code refinements.
  * Update wallpaper-con-citas to 1.0.7 version. It was necessary to correct an error related to \"Other authors.\" It only displays the following - No citations found. /Final revision.
  * Latest fixes to "wallpaper-con-citas" 1.0.6; Added writing "metadata" to image. Changed so that it does not overwrite if the quote is changed. And it was fixed at the Quote Edition in the image, more stable.
  * Add a transparent option to text background. And fix the "Write the Picture" function.
  * The up to date of wallpaper-con-citas, on version (1.0.4)
  * The up to date of wallpaper-con-citas, on version (1.0.3)
  * Remove the creation and handling of user-specific folders from the postinst script to avoid permission conflicts (PermissionError) with configuration directories such as ~/.config/wallpaper_manager.
  * Restrict permission adjustments to the system-wide shared path (/usr/share/wallpaper_manager/) only.
  * Correct the installation path in debian/wallpaper-manager.install using - wall-manager/* to avoid directory duplication.
  * Adjust the postinst script to ensure correct permissions and ownership - upon completion of package configuration.
  * Now, Citas & Wallpapers images can be downloaded from additional servers, such as pixabay.com and www.pexels.com. We also have a comprehensive «Otros autores» list—downloaded just once—that simplifies the process of searching for authors and retrieving citations.
